{%- doc -%}
  The run of detail cards down the product column (Figma: Standart Product Page →
  Ingredients & Allergens, Storage).

  The cards below are the template's default, the ones every product shows unless it
  says otherwise. A product says otherwise through the metafield named in
  `metafield` — a list of `detail_panel` entries, each carrying a title, a glyph, the
  line that stays visible and the copy behind the caret.

  A list, and one metafield, because these are a list. It used to be four fields —
  a summary and a body for each of two fixed cards — which is the numbered run
  `docs/section-settings.md` §0 warns about: a merchant could not add a third card,
  reorder them, or drop one. Now they can, and the count went from four to one.

  Entries reuse well where the words do: a Storage card that reads the same on every
  treat is one entry pointed at from every product, while an ingredients list is an
  entry of its own.
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign key = block.settings.metafield
  assign entries = ''
  if key != blank
    assign field = closest.product.metafields.custom[key]
    if field.type == 'list.metaobject_reference'
      assign entries = field.value
    endif
  endif
-%}

<div
  class="ui-product-panels"
  style="--ui-product-panels-gap: {{ block.settings.gap }}px;"
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
>
  {%- if entries.size > 0 -%}
    {%- for entry in entries -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        The body is rich text, and neither `.value` nor the field itself gives
        back markup here — both print the parsed tree, so the card ended up with
        a page of JSON on it. `metafield_tag` is what renders it, and it wraps
        the copy in a div of its own. Captured, because the card tests `body`
        with `blank` and a drop would not answer that honestly.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- capture panel_body -%}{{ entry.body | metafield_tag }}{%- endcapture -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        `icon` is a readable name off a choice list; `custom_icon` takes an asset
        name for the glyphs the list does not offer, and being the more specific
        of the two it wins when it is filled.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign entry_icon = entry.custom_icon.value | default: entry.icon.value -%}
      {% render 'ui-detail-card',
        title: entry.title.value,
        icon: entry_icon,
        summary: entry.summary.value,
        body: panel_body,
        collapsible: true
      %}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {% content_for 'blocks' %}
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{% stylesheet %}
  .ui-product-panels {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--ui-product-panels-gap, 12px);
  }

  /* The region has to be in the markup for the editor even when the metafield has
     taken over, and an empty flex item would still take its share of the column. */
  .ui-product-panels:not(:has(*)) {
    display: none;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Detail cards",
  "tag": null,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "_ui-product-panel"
    }
  ],
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "metafield",
      "label": "Per-product cards",
      "info": "A custom.* list of detail_panel metaobject entries. Filled in on a product, it replaces the cards below for that product.",
      "default": "detail_panels"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap",
      "label": "t:settings.gap",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 32,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 12
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Detail cards"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
